BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/g5qqma-sloppy-jane-11th-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Sloppy Jane
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260811T230000
UID:5a04a4779df6def31aba14c0583f2676@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, August 11 Sloppy Jane w/ Cherub Tree Sloppy Jane is 
 the creative and artist project of Haley Dahl. 2021 saw the release of the
  critically acclaimed chamber pop/rock album Madison on Saddest Factory Re
 cords. The album and accompanying visual album were recorded entirely in a
  cave in West Virginia\, and the music features stunning orchestral arrang
 ements by Dahl. Dahl currently performs with an up-to 10-piece band and pu
 ts on a singularly captivating and frenetic live show. The band has shared
  stages with boygenius\, Iceage\, Pussy Riot: Riot Days\, Deap Vally\, CSS
 \, Bartees Strange\, Phoebe Bridgers\, and more. Last year an original son
 g by Sloppy Jane ft. Phoebe Bridgers was featured on the soundtrack for th
 e A24 film I Saw The TV Glow\, directed by Jane Schoenbrun and premiered a
 t the Sundance Film Festival. Dahl is currently composing a feature film s
 core and working on writing the next Sloppy Jane album. \\*\\*\\* Fronted 
 by Brenna Dascoulias and guitarist Ryan Shakeri with support from drummer 
 Sam Elliott and bassist Izzy Burke\, Cherub Tree are a bubblegrunge band t
 hat specializes in music that has both a soft indie rock sound and a harde
 r punk edge. Learning to balance the two genres took years of dedication\,
  but they’ve managed to pull it off. “Bubblegrunge is a fitting term f
 or our versatility\,” Shakeri says. “We’re able to combine alternati
 ve and punk music while making it feel cohesive.”
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/g5qqma-sloppy-jane-11th-aug-songbyrd-washington-
 dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
