BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/eox2d2-the-exchange-project-20th-aug-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:The Exchange Project
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260820T230000
UID:031128f22737c447c77d4d52fbf27cd5@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Thursday August 20th The Exchange Project w/ R-NOT\, Please Kn
 ock \\*\\*\\* The Exchange Project is a Washington\, DC based rock band. W
 ith members hailing from Caracas\, Venezuela\, La Serena\, Chile\, Fort Wo
 rth\, TX and Cleveland\, OH\, The Exchange Project combines high-energy fu
 zz drenched guitar\, intricate bass lines\, apocalyptic drums and vocals t
 hat go from soulful baritone to full-out rock and roll snarl in less than 
 a blink of your bloodshot eye. TXP will continue releasing original music 
 in between studio sessions and playing the local DC music scene. \\*\\*\\*
  From the suburban reaches of Washington DC\, R-NØT is a high-energy punk
 -inspired rock trio. Prolific punk singer/songwriter Paul Makarov teams up
  Chuck Bowley (bass guitar) and Mike Packard (drums) to unleash a barrage 
 of punky\, chunky\, yet highly melodic tunes that conjure up your inner an
 gsty teenager. With a vibe reminiscent of a bygone era\, their short\, swe
 et\, raw and powerful songs simply get stuck in your head. \\*\\*\\* Drawi
 ng on everything from grunge to heavy metal\, Northern Virginia alt-rock o
 utfit Please Knock formed as longtime friends Zach Piner (vocals/guitar) a
 nd Chris 'CPZ' Peele (drums) reunited after a college degree and brief sti
 nt in the military. Along with 2024 additions Mark Conigliaro (bass) and C
 hristian Sheets (guitar)\, they bring heavy\, soulful music boasting equal
  parts melody and aggression.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/eox2d2-the-exchange-project-20th-aug-songbyrd-wa
 shington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
