X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/6dox7q-riot-grrrls-not-dead-dc-9th-oct-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:Riot Grrrl's Not Dead DC!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T230000
UID:737341ba74c2e09b97b6e2875d68d95d@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:Friday October 9th Riot Grrrl's Not Dead DC! ft. Cat Crash\, B
 uko Buko\, Ammonite\, Bitter Tits \\*\\*\\* Cat Crash is a punk band from 
 NYC/CT/NJ/MA and we have nine lives. We blend 90s riot grrrl\, 2000s pop p
 unk\, and 2010s midwest emo\, touring across several states and opening fo
 r bands such as Skating Polly\, Pinkshift\, VIAL. We are all-trans and Asi
 an-fronted and committed to uplifting and supporting people of color\, que
 er people\, and femme people. \\*\\*\\* DC-based BUKO BUKO is a happy punk
  band born out of boredom from sad\, soggy\, serious punk music and fueled
  by Riot Grrrl and mean mommy energy. BUKO BUKO live shows are an experien
 ce to laugh\, dance\, and mosh. They don bright colors and cheap wigs\, fe
 ed fans gummy worms\, and get the crowd moshing to songs like “Spaghetti
  Time.” BUKO BUKO’s debut album\, titled All You Can Eat\, was release
 d as a labor of love (literally) to "bring feral joy to the mosh pit\," as
  Washington Post writes. Their song topics range from food metaphors to im
 migrant manifestos and they're known for their banter and crazy dance move
 s. BUKO BUKO means “young coconut” in Tagalog and is a nod to the sing
 er’s half-Filipino heritage. \\*\\*\\* Like heartland folk with a switch
 blade in its boot\, Ammonite comes out swinging. Sweeping audiences away o
 n a musical adventure marked with rolling emotional hills and lyrical reve
 lations. The trio offers up Queer Americana for people who grew up on punk
 . Delivered with tension\, dynamic\, and outstanding vocals and guitar fro
 m the couple at the heart of the group - Erin Frisby (they\,them) and Sele
 na Benally (she\,her)\, Ammonite is a full band explosion of something mem
 orable\, sometimes visceral\, vulnerable\, and cathartic. It's virtuosic s
 ongwriting and playing that still manages to capture all of the thrill and
  spontaneity of a basement show. \\*\\*\\* Bitter Tits is a punk rock duo 
 based out of Baltimore and we play punk rock\, we sing the stories of our 
 lives and apologize for nothing the world is what made us who we are. We
 ’re here to help you get by\, we’re to help you forget\, we’re here 
 to help you remember\, and we’re here to party with the masses.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/6dox7q-riot-grrrls-not-dead-dc-9th-oct-songbyrd-
 washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
