BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/53mn7d-june-mcdoom-23rd-oct-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:June McDoom
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261023T230000
UID:f0699628a581cf7c3b25b9c57e28807c@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:There is a hush most of us only knew as children\, the warm dr
 ift between familiar household sounds and being carried to bed\, a place t
 hat belongs to you and to some self you have not met yet. June McDoomʼs d
 ebut full-length\, Follow the Light\, lives in that dream space and then k
 eeps walking\, slipping out of time and waking somewhere new\, barely fami
 liar enough to feel like home yet wholly your own. She came up in a Jamaic
 an household on the edge of the Florida Everglades\, an existence built of
  extended family\, communal care\, bass and harmonics. Her father\, a carp
 enter and a student of sound\, built his own speakers and kept three sound
  systems going across as many rooms. His low end would rise through her be
 droom floor like some wayward cat while she lay above it with folk records
 \, finding harmonies that were new and hers alone. Two musics in one room.
  Lushness as past and premonition. She found folk on her own\, somewhere b
 etween the cast recording of The Sound of Music and Simon and Garfunkel\, 
 while everyone around her called it sleepy music. She did not mind being t
 he only one. The solitude let her fall for harmony first\, before words\, 
 before anything else\, and harmony is still the thing she reaches for. Gen
 erationally speaking\, the music was already in the air. Her grandfather\,
  Colin Smith\, is a distinguished mento man who played banjo and guitar an
 d built his own rumba boxes\, worked to keep Jamaicaʼs oldest acoustic fo
 lk form alive. Mento is the root of all of it: ska\, rock steady\, reggae\
 , dub and everything after. He is the one who put a guitar in her hands. A
 n inheritance\, a gift and a map. Even her name is part of it\, though she
  will tell you she landed on it more by feel than reason. She records as J
 une McDoom\, born Alyssa\, June being a nickname one of her grandmothers\,
  Joan\, went by\, a name she thought was cool to carry and simply liked th
 e sound of. An etheric channel that reverberates all the same. A dub all i
 ts own. Made slowly and by hand with her longtime partner Evan Wright\, Fo
 llow the Light lays the harmony of folk over the rhythm of dub\, with Dion
 ne Warwick\, Minnie Riperton\, Pentangle and the washed guitars of Cocteau
  Twins haunting its outer edges. Voice and guitar seeking each other out f
 irst\, then everything else stacked across long days in the studio they ke
 ep at home\, restraint kept on purpose. The lead single “Without You” 
 is the whole method surfacing\, split open and sparkling like a geode in a
  creek bed. Angelic heroics\, and nothing less.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/53mn7d-june-mcdoom-23rd-oct-songbyrd-washington-
 dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
