BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Songbyrd Music House": "https://dice.fm/event/q2l9mp-natanya-the-attitude-tour-7th-nov-songbyrd-washington-dc-tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:songbyrd
SUMMARY:NATANYA - THE ATTITUDE TOUR
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261107T230000
UID:1f0c08492706944daa2783e681105cd5@songbyrddc.com
DESCRIPTION:London-based singer-songwriter and producer Natanya is emergin
 g as one of pop’s most compelling new voices\, crafting music that blend
 s emotional candor with sharp\, self-assured production. Raised in North W
 est London\, she began playing classical piano at just four years old and 
 quickly discovered her perfect pitch\, later refining her musicianship at 
 the Julian Joseph Jazz Academy. Early influences spanning Janet Jackson\, 
 Amy Winehouse\, Paramore\, and Stevie Wonder helped shape her genre-fluid 
 sensibility. While studying English Literature at University College Londo
 n\, Natanya wrote and produced her debut project\, Sorrow at Sunrise (2023
 )\, a coming-of-age tape structured as a series of diaristic reflections. 
 She expanded her sonic world with the dual EP releases Feline’s Return w
 ith lead singles Daydream\, Dangerous\,\, Guitar\, and Feline’s Return A
 ct II with lead singles Jezebel \, Meeting You Once (The End)\, On Ur Time
  and Sofa Joy all of which gained significant momentum from the release. M
 arking a confident shift toward a more polished\, pop-forward sound withou
 t losing her introspective edge. Her latest single\, “DON’T ASK!”\, 
 encapsulates this evolution-a bold\, self-possessed anthem centered on age
 ncy and ambition. Natanya’s next single\, “CANDYLAND!”\, is set for 
 release in June\, ahead of a new project arriving in September. Across her
  work\, Natanya serves as the executive producer and sole lyricist\, with 
 Oscar Scheller acting as co-producer. Natanya’s rise has been met with e
 arly acclaim and co-signs from artists including SZA\, Tyler\, The Creator
 \, Clairo\, and RAYE. A captivating live performer\, she has toured with D
 estin Conrad\, Ravyn Lenae\, Mereba and supported FLO and PinkPantheress. 
 With a growing global fanbase and an instinct for reinvention\, Natanya is
  carving out a lane entirely her own. Natanya’s music has received early
  yet abundant critical acclaim. She won GUAP GALA’s “Music Artist to W
 atch” award in 2023\, an honor previously given to the girl group FLO. S
 he has also been featured in many magazines such as\; Paper\, Pitchfork\, 
 Clash\, NME\, Dazed.
LOCATION:Songbyrd\, 540 Penn St NE\, Washington\, DC 20002\, USA
URL:https://dice.fm/event/q2l9mp-natanya-the-attitude-tour-7th-nov-songbyr
 d-washington-dc-tickets
X-SOURCE:Songbyrd
END:VEVENT
